From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 02:42:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] model(caiso): measured battery AS-award reservation +
 2023 demand-clock realignment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

caiso_storage_as_reservation (default off): reserve the measured hourly
battery upward-AS award (reg_up+spin+nonspin) from the battery power cap
pro-rata (the ERCOT storage_as_commitment pattern, batteries only) and
floor battery SOC at the tariff 30-min sustain of the spin/nonspin award
(CAISO_AS_SUSTAIN_DURATION_H, the reserve co-opt's own constant). New
storage_soc_min bound threaded through build_variable_bounds /
DispatchModel / solve_dispatch / DispatchSpec (UNSET-omitted). Zero
fitted parameters; mutually exclusive with energy_reserve_coopt
(validator, rule 19).

caiso_demand_clock_realign (default off): the EIA-930 CISO Demand column
rides +1h late vs the extract's own wall-true generation frame for local
dates before 2023-11-01 (monthly best-lag -1 at r 0.984-0.997 vs the
extract's balance identity; OASIS SLD corroborates at 0.9953) — realign
that window onto the model frame. Measured lag constants frozen against
residuals, guarded by scripts/validate_caiso_demand_clock.py.

Probe script _caiso74_storage_as_ab.py carries the pre-registered
directions. fetch_caiso_oasis gains the AS_RESULTS dataset registration
(cross-check denominator; not fetched in bulk).

